<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bletchley Park</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bletchley Park is a country house and estate in Buckinghamshire, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, that was the centre of British codebreaking during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. Thousands of staff, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alan-turing">Alan Turing</a>, broke German Enigma and Lorenz ciphers there, producing the intelligence known as Ultra, and the work led to Colossus, one of the first programmable electronic computers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bletchley-park.jpg" alt="Bletchley Park" width="320" height="188" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DeFacto · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bletchley_Park_Mansion.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
